Ported code notices
===================

Some source files are ported from other projects. Each such file starts with a provenance header
of the form

    provenance: port <project>@<tag>:<upstream-path> (<SPDX>)

and `cargo xtask check provenance` accepts it only when <project> is in the licence policy
(SymPy, mpmath, Diofant and FriCAS under BSD-3-Clause; SymEngine under MIT) and this file has a
block for it.

Each block starts with a line that is exactly `Project: {name}`, where {name} is the project name
used in the provenance headers (for example `Project: sympy`). The block then carries that
project's copyright and licence notice verbatim, as the upstream licence requires. A block is added
by the plan that lands the first port from that project.

There are no ported files yet, so there are no blocks below.
